iv class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">7.8<br/>August 1, 2006<br/>Summer Update 2006</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Hunting Places <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p><b>Talahu</b>, otherwise known as <a href=\"#/wiki/Hydra\">Hydra</a> Island, is as the alternate name would suggest, crawling with <a href=\"#/wiki/Hydra\">Hydras</a>. Talahu is much smaller than Fibula, yet contains around 20-30 Hydras on its surface making travel on the island very tricky for groups trying to get to <a href=\"#/wiki/Malada\">Malada</a> and later <a href=\"#/wiki/Kharos\">Kharos</a>. Talahu is a popular destination spot for high level mages seeking fast experience and decent cash. Talahu is also the only island with a <a href=\"#/wiki/Mailbox\">mailbox</a> inside the <a href=\"#/wiki/Teleportation%20Hub\">Teleportation Hub</a>. Talahu is the second island in the teleportation chain. \nBelow Talahu one can find a maze of caves with all different Quara scouts and Bog Raiders. Two floors below there is a square maze containing Quara scouts which makes a nice hunting spot for players of level 120 and above.\nTo the north of this maze is a gate of expertise leading to <a href=\"#/wiki/Medusa%20Cave\">a cave</a> with <a href=\"#/wiki/Serpent%20Spawn\">Serpent Spawns</a> and <a href=\"#/wiki/Medusa\">Medusae</a>.\n</p><p><br/>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><caption>Talahu Creatures</caption><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">Exp</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">HP</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">Max. Damage</th><th style=\"font-size: small;\">Loot</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 100px; text-align: center\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><sp